# One round of tcc compiling itself -- the PE32 counterpart of
# boot-round.kaem beside this.
#
# No `cd ${TMPDIR}`: every other Windows kaem script in this chain avoids
# it the same way, naming paths explicitly instead -- kaem's cd is a
# native chdir(), and nothing on this side has proven that call behaves
# the way this build needs under the exec-wrapper this chain builds
# through. config.h goes into ${out}/bin (created first) rather than a
# cwd that was never changed into, and -I names that directory instead
# of `.`.
#
# Two more differences, both because tccpe.c and tccelf.c disagree about
# what "the usual libraries" means and neither of boot-round.kaem's two
# ways of getting them is this format's:
#
# crt1.o is never added automatically for TCC_TARGET_PE the way
# libtcc.c's tcc_add_crt calls add it for ELF (that whole block is
# `#else` from `#ifdef TCC_TARGET_PE`) -- so it is named on the command
# line here as an ordinary input file, the same as tcc.c itself.
#
# TCC_LIBGCC and CONFIG_USE_LIBGCC, which pull libc.a in automatically on
# the ELF side, are read only by tccelf.c and never even compiled into a
# PE-target tcc -- so are the very definitions of "the usual libraries"
# tccpe.c reaches for on its own instead, but tccpe.c's own idea of that
# is msvcrt.dll, kernel32.dll, user32.dll and gdi32.dll: real Windows
# import libraries this bootstrap has no counterpart for and does not
# want, having reached every one of ntdll's exports through the PEB
# instead since before tcc.c could compile at all. -nostdlib turns that
# whole default off, and -L/-lc/-ltcc1 name what this side actually has
# in its place.
#
# -U _WIN32 and -D __windows__=1, which look contradictory and are not.
# _WIN32 is what a PE-configured tcc defines, and tcc.h reads it as "the
# machine tcc is running on is Windows", taking a branch that includes
# <windows.h>, <io.h> and <direct.h> and renames snprintf to _snprintf.
# None of that is true here: tcc runs on Windows but against mes-libc,
# which is POSIX-shaped and has none of those headers -- the #ifndef
# _WIN32 branch, unistd.h and sys/time.h, is the one that fits.  So the
# host half of that macro is turned off, and __windows__ -- what the rest
# of this bootstrap already passes, see stage0-pe32's m2-program.nix --
# tells mes's own fcntl.h which system it is.  TCC_TARGET_PE is untouched
# and keeps deciding everything about the target, PATHSEP included.

${bin_mkdir} -p ${out}/bin
${bin_catm} ${out}/bin/config.h

${prevTcc} -B ${prevLibs}/lib -g -v -o ${out}/bin/tcc -U _WIN32 -D __windows__=1 -D BOOTSTRAP=1 ${opt1} ${opt2} ${opt3} ${opt4} ${opt5} ${opt6} ${opt7} ${opt8} -I ${out}/bin -I ${src} -D TCC_TARGET_${tccTarget}=1 -D CONFIG_TCCDIR=\"\" -D CONFIG_SYSROOT=\"\" -D CONFIG_TCC_CRTPREFIX=\"{B}\" -D CONFIG_TCC_ELFINTERP=\"\" -D CONFIG_TCC_LIBPATHS=\"{B}\" -D CONFIG_TCC_SYSINCLUDEPATHS=${sysIncludePaths} -D TCC_LIBGCC=\"libc.a\" -D TCC_LIBTCC1=\"libtcc1.a\" -D CONFIG_TCCBOOT=1 -D CONFIG_TCC_STATIC=1 -D CONFIG_USE_LIBGCC=1 -D TCC_MES_LIBC=1 -D TCC_VERSION=\"0.9.28-${version}\" -D ONE_SOURCE=1 -nostdlib ${prevLibs}/lib/crt1.o ${src}/tcc.c -L ${prevLibs}/lib -lc -ltcc1
